    "### 1.2.3 - Load Duration Curve\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0f57bdfd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The load duration curve is a commonly used representation of the distribution of power demand, where the demand data is ordered in descending order of magnitude, rather than chronologically.\n",
    "\n",
    "Typically, it is often used to plot the load across one year. It helps identify the peak load and baseload."
   ]
  },
