  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ac2ba13c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.2 - Controllable generation technologies (overview)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "98d2c5f4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "There are two main categories of controllable generation technologies:\n",
    "- **Baseload power plants**: Capital intensive, with inertia, but cheap to run. They are used to cover the baseload, as they need to run long enough to be economically efficient.\n",
    "- **Peak load power plants**: OPEX intensive, but low CAPEX and modular. They are used to cover the peakloads, as they can be started quickly, and should be running to long as they are expensive.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Among all existing technologies, based on ERAA data, we consider here:\n",
    "- **Nuclear**: typical baseload (technical & economic)\n",
    "- **Biomass**: usually peakload (economic)\n",
    "- **Oil**: typical peakload (economic)\n",
    "- **Combined Cycle Gas Turbine (CCGT)**: usually baseload (technical)\n",
    "- **Open Cycle Gas Turbine (OCGT)**: usually peakload (economic)\n",
    "- **Hard Coal**: usually baseload (technical)\n",
    "- **Lignite**: usually baseload (technical)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**Remark**: Storage assets, such as hydro reservoirs and pumped hydro or batteries, can also be considered as controllable technologies, but are not considered in this data crunch session. Storage assets require more advanded modelling. ***We will discuss storage on Wednesday***"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "44f5a241",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.3 - Economic and environmental characteristics of controllable technologies\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6baea7a0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In this subsection we are going to investigate the main characteristics of the considered technologies:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2c5627fc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- **Environmental**: CO2eq emissions\n",
    "- **Economic**:\n",
    "    - <u>**Fixed cost**, annualized, include:</u>\n",
    "        - Investment costs (CAPEX)\n",
    "        - Cost of capital (WACC)\n",
    "        - Fixed O&M costs (FOM)\n",
    "\n",
    "    - <u>**Variable costs** include:</u>\n",
    "        - Fuel Cost\n",
    "        - CO2 taxes\n",
    "        - Efficiency\n",
    "        - Variable O&M costs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b593d5f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 2.3.1 - Fixed costs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0f261530",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To be able to analyze FOM & CAPEX together, include cost of capital, and compare technologies with different operational lifespan, we need to annualize the costs first "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "99e899c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cost of Capital + CAPEX computation function\n",
    "def vpm(rate, nper, pv, fv=0, type=0):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Replicates the Standard Excel VPM function(rate; nper; va; [vc]; [type])\n",
    "\n",
    "    rate : rate per period\n",
    "    nper : total number of period\n",
    "    pv   : present value (e.g. amount borrowed)\n",
    "    fv   : future value (e.g. accumulated capital) [optional]\n",
    "    type : 0 = payment at the end of the period, 1 = start of the period\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if rate == 0:\n",
    "        return (pv + fv) / nper\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return (rate * (pv * (1 + rate)**nper + fv)/((1 + rate * type) * ((1 + rate)**nper - 1)))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 29,
   "id": "b1382021",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ---- Load economic data JSON files ----\n",
    "with open(\"data/fuel_sources/technology_datacrunch.json\", \"r\") as f:\n",
    "    tech_data = json.load(f)\n",
    "with open(\"data/fuel_sources/fuels_datacrunch.json\", \"r\") as f:\n",
    "    fuel_data = json.load(f)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "a573addb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ---- Compute fixed annual costs ----\n",
    "fixed_costs = {}\n",
    "fixed_costs_repartition = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for tech, vals in tech_data.items():\n",
    "    capex = vals.get(\"CAPEX\")\n",
    "    lifetime = vals.get(\"Lifetime\")\n",
    "    wacc = vals.get(\"WACC\")\n",
    "    fom = vals.get(\"FOM\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    if capex is None or lifetime is None or wacc is None or fom is None:\n",
    "        # Renewable technologies have no CAPEX/WACC/Lifetime data in your JSON\n",
    "        fixed_costs[tech] = None\n",
    "        fixed_costs_repartition[tech] = None\n",
    "     \n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    \n",
    "    fixed_costs_repartition[tech] = {}\n",
    "    annualized_investment = vpm(wacc, lifetime, capex)\n",
    "    fixed_costs[tech] = annualized_investment + fom\n",
    "\n",
    "    fixed_costs_repartition[tech][\"invest_overnight\"] = capex/lifetime\n",
    "    fixed_costs_repartition[tech][\"capital\"] = annualized_investment - capex/lifetime\n",
    "    fixed_costs_repartition[tech][\"FOM\"] = fom"
   ]
  },
