   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9d223998",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Question:**\n",
    "- What happens if you change the price of CO2?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f9bb0667",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Your answer:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Higher CO₂ price → biomass replaces gas: biomass 4.0 → 5.7 → 6.5 GW, CCGT 2.1 → 1.1 → 0.6 GW (100 → 200 → 300 €/t)\n",
    "- Nuclear stays at ≈ 25 GW: neither nuclear nor biomass emits CO₂, so their break-even (≈ 4,760 h) doesn't move\n",
    "- Without a CO₂ price, biomass disappears and CCGT takes ≈ 7 GW (nuclear only 23 GW)\n",
    "- Coal and lignite are never optimal, even at 0 €/t (CCGT is always cheaper)"
   ]
  },
