  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c0c20490",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4.2 Impact of variable Renewable technologies on the demand"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "147ba7df",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "As variable renewable energies (vRES) are not dispatchable and not controllable, we need to assess how naturally each type of vRES contributes to the demand supply. As they have null marginal costs, they are almost always nominated in the merit order, which justifies this approach.\n",
    "\n",
    "To do so, we will examine for each type of vRES the net demand, which is total electricity demand (or gross demand), minus generation from this type of vRES."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fc0803b7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.2.1 Hydro RoR"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fd1d5dd1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Integrating the effect of hydro ROR**\n",
    "\n",
    "As the run of river (RoR) is not a capacity that one can develop as wished due to geographical constraints, we will only consider the capacities provided by the national TSOs, and will investigate what is the impact of Hydro run-of-river on the demand given this installed capacity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "61bf1da3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# 0. Setup:\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_year = 2025"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "03ee9b9e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create the hourly time series for hydro ROR, for each climatic year\n",
    "df_ror = pd.read_csv(ror_file, sep=\";\")\n",
    "df_ror[\"value\"] = pd.to_numeric(df_ror[\"value\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "df_ror = df_ror[df_ror[\"zone\"] == country_choice].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "hourly_index = pd.date_range(start=\"1900-01-01\", periods=8760, freq=\"h\")\n",
    "\n",
    "hydro_ROR_ts = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for year in ERAA_climatic_years:\n",
    "    df_year = df_ror[df_ror[\"climatic_year\"] == year].sort_values(\"day\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Expand daily values to hourly (uniform split: daily value / 24)\n",
    "    hourly_values = np.repeat(df_year[\"value\"].values / 24, 24)\n",
    "\n",
    "    key = f\"CY{year}\"\n",
    "    hydro_ROR_ts[key] = hourly_values\n",
    "\n",
    "hydro_ROR_ts = pd.DataFrame(hydro_ROR_ts, index=hourly_index) * 1000  # GW -> MW"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9da5cca7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ---- Step 1: net demand = gross demand - hydro RoR generation for each year and climatic year ----\n",
    "net_demand_hydroRoR = {}\n",
    "for year in ERAA_target_years:\n",
    "    gross_demand = demands[year]\n",
    "    gross_demand.columns = gross_demand.columns.astype(str)\n",
    "    hydro_ROR_ts.columns = hydro_ROR_ts.columns.astype(str)\n",
    "    for climatic_year in hydro_ROR_ts.columns:\n",
    "        if climatic_year in gross_demand.columns:\n",
    "            gross = gross_demand[climatic_year]\n",
    "            hydro = hydro_ROR_ts[climatic_year]\n",
    "            # Subtract by position (.values), not by index label, since\n",
    "            # gross_demand is indexed on real `year` dates while\n",
    "            # hydro_ROR_ts is indexed on a fixed reference year (1900).\n",
    "            net_hydroRoR = pd.Series(gross.values - hydro.values, index=gross.index, name=climatic_year)\n",
    "            if year not in net_demand_hydroRoR:\n",
    "                net_demand_hydroRoR[year] = {}\n",
    "            net_demand_hydroRoR[year][climatic_year] = net_hydroRoR\n",
    "           \n",
    "# ---- Step 2: net load duration curve for each year and climatic year (unchanged) ----\n",
    "net_ldc_hydroRoR = {}\n",
    "for year in net_demand_hydroRoR:\n",
    "    net_ldc_hydroRoR[year] = {}\n",
    "    for climatic_year in net_demand_hydroRoR[year]:\n",
    "        net_ldc_hydroRoR[year][climatic_year] = pd.Series(\n",
    "            net_demand_hydroRoR[year][climatic_year].sort_values(ascending=False).values,\n",
    "            name=climatic_year\n",
    "        ).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "    net_ldc_hydroRoR[year] = pd.DataFrame(net_ldc_hydroRoR[year])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bccd0ad1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ---- Plot LDC (dashed) and net LDC (solid) for the climatic year selected for the notebook, target year ----\n",
    "\n",
    "climatic_years = [Notebook_climatic_year]\n",
    "\n",
    "palette = pc.qualitative.Plotly  # or any other qualitative palette\n",
    "color_map = {cy: palette[i % len(palette)] for i, cy in enumerate(climatic_years)}\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = go.Figure()\n",
    "\n",
    "for cy in climatic_years:\n",
    "    color = color_map[cy]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Gross LDC (dashed)\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(\n",
    "        go.Scatter(\n",
    "            x=ldc[plot_year].index,\n",
    "            y=ldc[plot_year][cy] / 1e3,\n",
    "            mode=\"lines\",\n",
    "            #name=f\"{cy} — gross\",\n",
    "            name = \"Gross demand\",\n",
    "            line=dict(color=color, dash=\"dot\"),\n",
    "            legendgroup=cy,\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Net LDC (solid)\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(\n",
    "        go.Scatter(\n",
    "            x=net_ldc_hydroRoR[plot_year].index,\n",
    "            y=net_ldc_hydroRoR[plot_year][cy] / 1e3,\n",
    "            mode=\"lines\",\n",
    "            # name=f\"{cy} — net\",\n",
    "            name = \"Net demand of hydro run-of-river\",\n",
    "            line=dict(color=color, dash=\"solid\"),\n",
    "            legendgroup=cy,\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.update_layout(\n",
    "    title=f\"Gross vs Net of hydro RoR Load Duration Curves — {plot_year} - {country_choice}\",\n",
    "    xaxis_title=\"Hours\",\n",
    "    yaxis_title=\"Demand (GW)\",\n",
    "    template=\"plotly_white\",\n",
    "    hovermode=\"x unified\",\n",
    "   # legend_title=\"Climatic year\",\n",
    "    width=1100,\n",
    "    height=600,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "799eae91",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Questions:**\n",
    "- Does Hydro ROR contribute to the security of supply equally during all year?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eec66885",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Your answer:**\n",
    "\n",
    "_Double-click here to enter your answer_\n",
    "\n",
    "- "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c872bb0b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "***From now on, we will consider that hydro ROR is fatal, and work based on the demand, net of hydro ROR generation***"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cba35ae8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.2.2 Solar PV"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9abc1488",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Integrating the effect of solar PV**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6dcba275",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "What happens if you start adding more and more solar on the system? Let's investigate that question through the prism of net load duration curve"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2b803a27",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# 0. Setup: choose solar capacities to test\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "solar_pv_capacities = np.arange(0, 52500, 2500)  # MW, 0 to 50000 MW... wait, 50 GW, step 2.5 GW\n",
    "zoom_hours_low = 0 # low boundary for scarcity hours to zoom in for analysis\n",
    "zoom_hours_high = 100 # downward boudary for scarciest hours to zoom in for analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_year = 2025"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ab12ea4a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# 1. Load solar PV capacity factors, build hourly matrix aligned with net_demand\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "res_capacity_folder = \"data/ERAA_2023-2/res_capa-factors\"\n",
    "solar_file = f\"{res_capacity_folder}/capa_factor_solar_pv_{plot_year}_{country_choice}.csv\"\n",
    "target_cy = Notebook_climatic_year\n",
    "\n",
    "df_solar = pd.read_csv(solar_file, sep=\";\")\n",
    "df_solar[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df_solar[\"date\"])\n",
    "df_solar[\"value\"] = pd.to_numeric(df_solar[\"value\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "\n",
    "solar_cf = df_solar.pivot_table(index=\"date\", columns=\"climatic_year\", values=\"value\").sort_index()\n",
    "solar_cf.columns = [f\"CY{cy}\" for cy in solar_cf.columns]  # match net_demand column naming\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# 2. Compute net demand with increasing solar PV, for the target climatic year\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "base_net_demand = net_demand_hydroRoR[plot_year][target_cy]  # Series, MW, indexed on target_year real dates\n",
    "\n",
    "net_demands_hydro_solarPV = {}\n",
    "for capa in solar_pv_capacities:\n",
    "    net_demands_hydro_solarPV[capa] = pd.Series(\n",
    "        base_net_demand.values - capa * solar_cf[target_cy].values,\n",
    "        index=base_net_demand.index\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# 3. Net load duration curves per solar capacity\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "net_ldc_hydro_solarPV = {}\n",
    "for capa in solar_pv_capacities:\n",
    "    df = net_demands_hydro_solarPV[capa].copy()\n",
    "    net_ldc_hydro_solarPV[capa] = df.sort_values(ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = go.Figure()\n",
    "for capa in solar_pv_capacities:\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(\n",
    "        go.Scatter(\n",
    "            x=net_ldc_hydro_solarPV[capa].index,\n",
    "            y=net_ldc_hydro_solarPV[capa] / 1e3,\n",
    "            mode=\"lines\",\n",
    "            name=f\"{int(capa/1000)} GW\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.update_layout(\n",
    "    title=f\"Impact of Solar PV on Net Load Duration Curves – {plot_year} - {country_choice}\",\n",
    "    xaxis_title=\"Hours\",\n",
    "    yaxis_title=\"Net Demand (GW)\",\n",
    "    template=\"plotly_white\",\n",
    "    hovermode=\"x unified\",\n",
    "    width=1100,\n",
    "    height=600,\n",
    "    legend_title=\"Solar Capacity\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\n",
    "    \"We can see that the impact is not the same on the hours with lowest and highest consumption! \"\n",
    "    \"Indeed, there usually is a significant correlation between solar production, the weather, and the demand!\\n\"\n",
    "    \"Let's push the analysis a step further to clearly observe the marginal impacts of adding solar PV in the mix!\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# 4. Marginal contribution of solar PV\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "baseline = net_ldc_hydro_solarPV[0].values\n",
    "net_ldc_diff_hydro_solarPV = {}\n",
    "for capa in solar_pv_capacities:\n",
    "    net_ldc_diff_hydro_solarPV[capa] = (baseline - net_ldc_hydro_solarPV[capa].values) / 1e3\n",
    "\n",
    "x = np.arange(len(baseline))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = go.Figure()\n",
    "for capa in solar_pv_capacities:\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(\n",
    "        go.Scatter(\n",
    "            x=x,\n",
    "            y=net_ldc_diff_hydro_solarPV[capa],\n",
    "            mode=\"lines\",\n",
    "            name=f\"{round(capa/1000, 1)} GW\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.update_layout(\n",
    "    title=f\"Marginal Net Load Reduction from Solar – {plot_year} - {country_choice}\",\n",
    "    xaxis_title=\"Hour Rank (Load Duration Curve)\",\n",
    "    yaxis_title=\"Net Load Reduction (GW)\",\n",
    "    template=\"plotly_white\",\n",
    "    hovermode=\"x unified\",\n",
    "    width=1100,\n",
    "    height=600,\n",
    "    legend_title=\"Solar Capacity\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\n",
    "    \"It is even clearer now! How about zooming on a specific period and really highlighting \"\n",
    "    \"the marginal contribution of each additional GW of solar on the demand?\\n\"\n",
    "    \"Advice: let's start with the scarcest hours of the year, which are really the most important \"\n",
    "    \"to size the power mix and limit deficit!\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# 5. Average marginal value over the zoomed (scarcest) hours\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "avg_ws_reduction_solar_pv = {}\n",
    "for capa in solar_pv_capacities:\n",
    "    avg_ws_reduction_solar_pv[capa] = np.mean(net_ldc_diff_hydro_solarPV[capa][zoom_hours_low:zoom_hours_high])\n",
    "\n",
    "x_vals = [c / 1000 for c in solar_pv_capacities]\n",
    "y_vals = [avg_ws_reduction_solar_pv[c] for c in solar_pv_capacities]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = go.Figure()\n",
    "fig.add_trace(\n",
    "    go.Scatter(\n",
    "        x=x_vals,\n",
    "        y=y_vals,\n",
    "        mode=\"lines+markers\",\n",
    "        name=\"Average reduction\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "fig.update_layout(\n",
    "    title=(\n",
    "        f\"Value of Solar PV on {plot_year} Net Demand - {country_choice} \\n\"\n",
    "        f\"(Avg reduction over [{zoom_hours_low};{zoom_hours_high}] LDC hours)\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    xaxis_title=\"Installed Solar Capacity (GW)\",\n",
    "    yaxis_title=\"Average Net Load Reduction (GW)\",\n",
    "    template=\"plotly_white\",\n",
    "    width=900,\n",
    "    height=500\n",
    ")\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# 6. Extract the datetimes of the top net-load hours (before/after solar)\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "capa_test = [0, 5000, 10000, 15000, 20000]\n",
    "\n",
    "sorted_with_time = {}\n",
    "for c in capa_test:\n",
    "    # Sort WITHOUT resetting index → keep original timestamps\n",
    "    sorted_with_time[c] = net_demands_hydro_solarPV[c].sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "    top_hours_datetimes = sorted_with_time[c].index[zoom_hours_low:zoom_hours_high]\n",
    "    top_hours_values = sorted_with_time[c].values[zoom_hours_low:zoom_hours_high]\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\"\\n============================================\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Top {zoom_hours_high - zoom_hours_low} highest net-load hours for {plot_year} (Capa = {c/1000} GW)\")\n",
    "    print(\"============================================\")\n",
    "    for dt, val in zip(top_hours_datetimes, top_hours_values):\n",
    "        print(f\"{dt}  -->  {val/1e3:.2f} GW\")"
   ]
